{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Before the priest comes.</b> The reason it was necessary to say <b>the priest</b> is that without it, it would have sounded as though before he comes he gives orders — and accordingly there would be no obligation upon the priest to wait until he knows that they have definitely cleared out everything that is in the house. But by his saying ״the priest,״ he indicated that the word ״before״ has no connection with the mention of the priest in ״and he shall command,״ but is connected with ״and they shall clear,״ and understand." "<b>Everything that is in the house.</b> Meaning: everything that is in the house shall not become impure — rather they shall save everything, even small jugs, for HaShem has compassion even on the most insignificant money of Israel. And in this the verse gave a reason why HaShem commanded to clear out beforehand — for after all, even after the priest enters and sees the plague, the house is not impure until the priest leaves and locks it up; if so, there is no need to clear out before the priest comes, and they could clear out after the priest comes, before he locks it up. Therefore he said <b>so that it not defile everything that</b> etc. — meaning, for on the side that when the priest sees the plague that requires locking up, there is no permission to delay locking up at all; and on account of the haste they would forget even insignificant money. Therefore HaShem insisted on clearing out beforehand, for in this way nothing of everything that is in the house will become impure." "And our Sages, of blessed memory, said (Nega'im 12:5, and in Torat Kohanim) that the Holy One, blessed be He, had compassion only on earthenware vessels, for other vessels and garments can be remedied in the mikveh. And according to our approach, we added the explanation that the Holy One, blessed be He, has compassion even on small earthenware vessels that a person does not value."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:57:03.790637024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}